# The files under apps/ are published so that a launcher already downloaded can
# fetch a newer tool and run it. That copy is meant to be the SAME text as the
# one carried inside the build, so nothing here may be rewritten on the way in
# or out: with autocrlf on, git stored LF where the build wrote CRLF and the
# served file was ~1KB smaller than the local one - which also made the size
# check after a publish meaningless.
apps/** -text
